<title>USA: USAir to accept American tickets if pilots strike.</title>
<headline>USAir to accept American tickets if pilots strike.</headline>
<dateline>ARLINGTON, Va. 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>USAir Group Inc said on Friday it will accept AMR Corp unit American Airlines' ticketed passengers for travel to their original destination on USAir flights should American Airlines' pilots strike at midnight Friday EST/0500 Saturday GMT.</p>
<p>USAir said if seats are not available, tickets will be accepted for stand-by travel.</p>
<p>Passengers holding American Airlines electronic tickets also may travel on USAir but first must obtain a paper ticket from American, USAir said.</p>
<p>It said unticketed passengers wishing to travel USAir need to purchase USAir tickets at the applicable fare.</p>
</text>
